BEGIN:VEVENT
ORGANIZER;CN="CSSZ":mailto:info@cssz.ch
SUMMARY:Sightseeing trip to Ticino
DESCRIPTION:<strong>Event details:</strong> https://cssz.ch/events/ticino-trip/\n<strong>Location:</strong> <a href="https://maps.app.goo.gl/54efBHM6SkjFigLm9" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Lugano, Bellinzona</a>\n<strong>Coordinator:</strong> Ondřej Peterka (<a class="link" href="mailto:ondrej.peterka@email.cz" target="_blank" rel="noopener">ondrej.peterka@email.cz</a>, <a class="link" href="tel:&#43;41782382184">+41 78 238 21 84</a>)\n<strong>Registration:</strong> <a href="https://chat.whatsapp.com/FOfDPDLK9nFCJh96XDCgTd?mode=ems_copy_t" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Whatsapp Group</a>\n\n<p>Join us in exploring the beauty of Ticino, where picturesque lakeside towns meet colourful architecture and Mediterranean flair, and experience the unique blend of Swiss precision and Italian atmosphere. We will start with a walk through the old town of Lugano, followed by a boat ride on the lake. In the lakeside park we will have pizza for lunch and enjoy some ice cream, and those interested will also have the chance to swim in the lake. Then we will decide whether to stay longer in Lugano or continue to Bellinzona, where one can admire the medieval castles listed as a UNESCO World Heritage Site.</p>
UID:20251004T070000-ticino-trip@cssz.ch
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
DTSTAMP:20251004T000000
DTSTART:20251004T070000
DTEND:20251004T200000
LOCATION;ALTREP="https://maps.app.goo.gl/54efBHM6SkjFigLm9":Lugano, Bellinzona
URL:https://cssz.ch/events/ticino-trip/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
ORGANIZER;CN="CSSZ":mailto:info@cssz.ch
SUMMARY:General Assembly
DESCRIPTION:<strong>Event details:</strong> https://cssz.ch/events/general-assembly-hs25/\n<strong>Location:</strong> Online (registered members will get an invitation)\n<strong>Coordinator:</strong> Zdeněk Šnajdr (<a class="link" href="mailto:zdenek.snajdr@cssz.ch" target="_blank" rel="noopener">zdenek.snajdr@cssz.ch</a>, <a class="link" href="tel:&#43;41762254840">+41762254840</a>)\n\nOn September 26th we will host a General Assembly (GA). We will look back at our activities of the last year, discuss the direction the society should take and elect a new board. In addition, we will vote on the new version of the statutes.
